course: dictionary
lesson: 1828
title: Coastal: where land meets the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coastal is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It means on or near the coast, where the land meets the sea. «Rising seas caused by global warming make coastal erosion and flooding worse.» Erosion and flooding happen where land meets the sea, so coastal must be about the shore.
explain: Look inside the word: coast plus al. The ending al often turns a word into a describing word, like natural or musical, so coastal means to do with the coast. Try it in a phrase: «a coastal town» is a town by the sea. Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: Coastal can describe water and paths too. «Coastal waters» are the seas near the shore, and a coastal path follows the edge of the land by the sea. Near cliff edges and tides, coastal walks need care.
fact: Coastal is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a coastal town.
fact: «Coastal» means on or near the coast, where land meets the sea.
fact: «Coastal erosion» is when the sea wears away the land along the shore.
fact: Coastal areas, such as beaches and cliffs, are key topics in geography.
fact: Wild cabbage grows on European coastal cliffs, and farmers bred it into broccoli, cabbage, kale and more.
exercise: «Rising seas caused by global warming make coastal erosion and flooding worse.» What does coastal mean here? | Hot and dry like a desert | *On or near the coast, where land meets the sea | Very high up in the mountains | Far away from any water
exercise: «They crowd into river valleys, coastal plains and fertile lowlands.» Find one word that is about the coast. | fertile | *coastal | lowlands | river
exercise: Which walk is a coastal walk? | A walk through a dark forest, miles from any water | *A walk along a path beside the cliffs and the sea | A walk around a shopping centre | A walk up a snowy mountain
test: Which phrase means the seas near the shore? | Desert sand | *Coastal waters | River valley | Mountain snow
test: «Wild cabbage that grows on European coastal cliffs» tells you where wild cabbage grows. Where is that? | Deep under the ground | In hot deserts | On high mountains | *On cliffs by the sea
exam: Which is the best meaning of coastal? | Underground in caves | Inland and dry | Far from the sea | *On or near the coast, where land meets the sea
